      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "QUICK CRUNCH (1) finished third at Ballarat two runs back then performed admirably last start, making up plenty of ground in a sustained effort but just coming up short over 1609m at Cranbourne. Will enjoy a nice run from this favourable starting position. Finds a tougher race but a big run is on the cards. HUXHAM CHUBB (7) put the writing on the wall two runs ago then improved further last time out when she scored by 2.75 metres over 2100m at Charlton. Will need a bit of luck negotiating a very wide starting position. Meets a similar line up so she is capable of taking this out. JILLIBY KYMY LOU (2) didn't do a bad job when sixth over 1660m at Hamilton last time out. Each-way. GOLD IN PARIS (6) must be respected after scoring last start by 3 metres at Hamilton over 1660m.",
